<!-- ================= ABSTRAK ================= -->
<h1>Abstrak</h1>
<p><strong>RANCANG BANGUN LEARNING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (LMS) BERBASIS WEB MENGGUNAKAN METODE DESIGN AND DEVELOPMENT RESEARCH (DDR) DAN FRAMEWORK LARAVEL DI SMKN 9 GARUT</strong></p>
<p>Oleh: Asep Suryana (NIM 24572014006)</p>
<p>Proses akademik di SMKN 9 Garut &mdash; distribusi materi, presensi, penugasan, ujian, dan rekapitulasi nilai &mdash; masih dilakukan secara manual sehingga berdampak pada efisiensi waktu guru, transparansi informasi bagi siswa, dan akurasi data untuk kebutuhan pelaporan sekolah. Penelitian ini bertujuan merancang dan membangun sebuah Learning Management System (LMS) berbasis web yang menghubungkan tiga peran pengguna &mdash; Administrator, Guru, dan Siswa &mdash; dalam satu sistem terpadu. Penelitian menggunakan pendekatan <em>Design and Development Research</em> (DDR) Tipe 1 (Richey &amp; Klein, 2007) dengan empat tahap: Analysis, Design, Development, dan Evaluation. Pada tahap Analysis dirumuskan 27 kebutuhan fungsional dan 7 kebutuhan nonfungsional. Pada tahap Design dihasilkan Entity Relationship Diagram dengan 30 entitas domain serta diagram UML (use case, activity, sequence). Pada tahap Development, sistem diimplementasikan menggunakan framework Laravel 12 dan PHP 8.2, menghasilkan 49 controller, 28 model, dan 32 berkas migrasi basis data, dengan penerapan Role-Based Access Control tiga peran serta proteksi CSRF, XSS, dan SQL Injection. Pada tahap Evaluation, pengujian <em>black-box</em> terhadap 13 kasus uji &mdash; mencakup autentikasi, otorisasi, integritas data, dan akurasi penilaian otomatis pada 600 jawaban kuis serta 590 baris nilai &mdash; menunjukkan tingkat keberhasilan 100%. Pengujian juga menemukan dan berhasil memperbaiki satu cacat fungsional pada modul penghapusan data guru. <span style="background:#FFF2CC;">[&#9888; TODO: lengkapi kalimat hasil evaluasi penerimaan pengguna (UAT) setelah data kuesioner responden nyata terkumpul dan diolah, sesuai Bab IV subbab 4.4.2]</span>. Hasil penelitian menunjukkan bahwa metode DDR dapat diterapkan secara efektif dalam pengembangan sistem informasi pendidikan berbasis web.</p>
<p><strong>Kata kunci:</strong> Learning Management System, Design and Development Research, Laravel, Sistem Informasi Akademik, Black-Box Testing.</p>

<h1>Abstract</h1>
<p><strong>DEVELOPMENT OF A WEB-BASED LEARNING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (LMS) USING THE DESIGN AND DEVELOPMENT RESEARCH (DDR) METHOD AND THE LARAVEL FRAMEWORK AT SMKN 9 GARUT</strong></p>
<p>By: Asep Suryana (Student ID 24572014006)</p>
<p>Academic processes at SMKN 9 Garut &mdash; material distribution, attendance recording, assignments, examinations, and grade recapitulation &mdash; are still carried out manually, affecting teacher time efficiency, information transparency for students, and data accuracy for school reporting needs. This research aims to design and build a web-based Learning Management System (LMS) that connects three user roles &mdash; Administrator, Teacher, and Student &mdash; within one integrated system. The research uses the Design and Development Research (DDR) Type 1 approach (Richey &amp; Klein, 2007) with four stages: Analysis, Design, Development, and Evaluation. In the Analysis stage, 27 functional requirements and 7 non-functional requirements were formulated. In the Design stage, an Entity Relationship Diagram with 30 domain entities and UML diagrams (use case, activity, sequence) were produced. In the Development stage, the system was implemented using the Laravel 12 framework and PHP 8.2, resulting in 49 controllers, 28 models, and 32 database migration files, with three-role Role-Based Access Control and CSRF, XSS, and SQL Injection protection. In the Evaluation stage, black-box testing on 13 test cases &mdash; covering authentication, authorization, data integrity, and automatic grading accuracy across 600 quiz answers and 590 grade records &mdash; showed a 100% success rate. Testing also identified and successfully fixed one functional defect in the teacher-deletion module. <span style="background:#FFF2CC;">[&#9888; TODO: complete this sentence with User Acceptance Testing results once real respondent data is collected]</span>. The results show that the DDR method can be effectively applied in the development of web-based educational information systems.</p>
<p><strong>Keywords:</strong> Learning Management System, Design and Development Research, Laravel, Academic Information System, Black-Box Testing.</p>

